use "testing" ;
use "time" ;

\ Regression: cancelling a task blocked on a channel receive must remove it from
\ the channel's waiter list. A stale waiter entry let a later send re-wake the
\ task, enqueuing it a second time and resuming a coroutine that was no longer
\ suspended ("attempt to resume a coroutine that is not suspended"), wedging the
\ scheduler. This surfaced as an intermittent hang in the concurrent-connections
\ server test, whose semaphore acquire blocks a receive that cancel-task tears
\ down while handlers concurrently release permits.

"cancel unwires a channel-blocked receiver" test-section

[
  ch: 1 <buffered-channel> ;
  r: [ ch receive drop ] spawn ;
  10 milliseconds sleep  \ let r park in ch.waiting_receivers
  r cancel-task          \ must remove r from the channel's waiter list
  ch t swap send         \ a later send must buffer, not re-wake the gone r
  r await-terminal       \ r ends cancelled; no double-resume, no hang
  ch receive t "buffered send survived the cancel" assert=
] task-scope

"done" print-line
